<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23508" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-jūdĭcātus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		2. in-judico. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Unsentenced</i>, <i>not formally tried
				by a judge</i>: decem hominibus vitam eripis, indicta causa,
			injudicatis, incondemnatis, Cato ap. <i><span class="en">Gell. 13,
				24, 12</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Undecided</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">id injudicatum relinquo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 10, 1, 67</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">res,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 5, 10, 15</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
